          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SCFT"} Super-conformal field theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 2
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vertex+operator+algebra"} super vertex operator algebra
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+charge"} central charge
            15 this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
          %p
            May be regarded as a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"}> 2-spectral triple
            ” (see there for more), the 2-dimensional generalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
            describing the quantum mechanics of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+particles"} spinning particles
            (super-particles).
