          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory+vacuum"} perturbative string theory vacuum
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A basic but detailed exposition focusing on the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            (and the perspective of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triples"} 2-spectral triples
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FroehlichGawedzki93"} Fröhlich &amp; Gawedzki (1993)
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erik+Plauschinn"} Erik Plauschinn
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to Conformal Field Theory – With Applications to String Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 779
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-00450-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-00450-6
          %p Other accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lance+Dixon"}> Lance Dixon
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Ginsparg"} Paul Ginsparg
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Harvey"} Jeffrey Harvey
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat c = 1
                  Superconformal field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.slac.stanford.edu/cgi-wrap/getdoc/slac-pub-4515.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yasuyuki+Kawahigashi"}> Yasuyuki Kawahigashi
                ,
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 2
                  Superconformal Field Theory and Operator Algebras
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.rci.rutgers.edu/~yzhuang/math/papers/kawahigashi.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            Constructing D=2 SCFTs from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/error-correcting+codes"} error-correcting codes
            and a hint for a relation to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theo+Johnson-Freyd"} Theo Johnson-Freyd
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holomorphic SCFTs with small index
              %strong 74
              2 (2022) 573-601 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.00589"}> arXiv:1811.00589
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4153/S0008414X2100002X"} doi:10.4153/S0008414X2100002X
          %p
            further on the resulting
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genera"} elliptic genera
          %ul
            %li
              Kohki Kawabata, Shinichiro Yahagi,
              %em Elliptic genera from classical error-correcting codes
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.12592"}> arXiv:2308.12592
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#relation_to_2spectral_triples Relation to 2-spectral triples
          %p
            Discussion of D=2 SCFTs as a higher analog of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triples"}> 2-spectral triples
            ”, see there for more) is in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebras"} vertex operator algebras
            in
          %ul
            %li#FroehlichGawedzki93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"}> Jürg Fröhlich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"} Krzysztof Gawędzki
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal Field Theory and Geometry of Strings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9310187"} arXiv:hep-th/9310187
            %li#Soibelman11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+Soibelman"}> Yan Soibelman
                ,
                %em Collapsing CFTs, spaces with non-negative Ricci curvature and nc-geometry
                , in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
          %p
            and in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+nets"} conformal nets
            in
          %ul
            %li#CHKL09
              Sebastiano Carpi, Robin Hillier,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yasuyuki+Kawahigashi"} Yasuyuki Kawahigashi
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roberto+Longo"} Roberto Longo
              = succeed "," do
                %em Spectral triples and the super-Virasoro algebra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0811.4128"} arXiv:0811.4128
          %div
            %h3#2dCFTAsFunctorialQFTReferences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
